The doorbell rings, and I open the door.
Sabine comes into the flat with her little dog Bruno.
She is carrying his basket and a heavy bag.
My neighbour is going away for the weekend.
We are standing in the hallway.
"In the bag are his food, his lead and his favourite toy," Sabine explains quickly.
Then she strictly lists the rules for Bruno.
"You must go for walks with him on time," she says seriously.
"And Bruno is not allowed to sleep on the bed!"
I laugh and take the bag.
"Don't worry, I will take very good care of him," I reassure my friend.
I smile.
"I will feed him right away," I say.
"Thank you, Maya," she answers, relieved.
Sabine says a warm goodbye to us.
She strokes Bruno one more time and leaves.
